WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.295
Easy Greek Myths. Orpheus and Eurydice.

00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:06.904
Orpheus was the greatest singer the world has ever known.

00:00:06.904 --> 00:00:11.305
When he sang and played, wild animals lay down to listen.

00:00:11.305 --> 00:00:14.165
Even the trees and rocks moved closer.

00:00:14.165 --> 00:00:18.741
He married a young woman named Eurydice, and they were very happy.

00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:24.075
But soon after, a snake bit her foot as she walked in the grass, and she died.

00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:26.412
Orpheus could not live without her.

00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:29.559
He decided to do what no living man had done.

00:00:29.559 --> 00:00:33.335
He would go down to the country of the dead and bring her back.

00:00:33.335 --> 00:00:36.743
He walked down a long, dark path under the earth.

00:00:36.743 --> 00:00:38.489
He sang as he went.

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:43.056
The boatman who carries the dead across the black river let him pass.

00:00:43.056 --> 00:00:46.831
The terrible dog with three heads lay down and slept.

00:00:46.831 --> 00:00:52.011
At last he stood in front of Hades, the king of the dead, and his queen.

00:00:52.011 --> 00:00:55.051
Orpheus sang about his love for Eurydice.

00:00:55.051 --> 00:00:58.125
The song was so sad that the queen cried.

00:00:58.125 --> 00:01:01.248
Even the hard face of the king became soft.

00:01:01.248 --> 00:01:03.849
"You may take her back," said Hades.

00:01:03.849 --> 00:01:05.710
"She will walk behind you.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:09.960
But you must not look at her until you are both in the light of the sun.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.023
If you turn around, you will lose her forever."

00:01:13.023 --> 00:01:15.507
Orpheus climbed the long path up.

00:01:15.507 --> 00:01:18.018
He could not hear her steps behind him.

00:01:18.018 --> 00:01:19.404
Was she really there?

00:01:19.404 --> 00:01:21.265
He walked on and on.

00:01:21.265 --> 00:01:23.335
At last he saw the light.

00:01:23.335 --> 00:01:27.890
He stepped out into the sun, and he was so happy that he turned around.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:30.462
But Eurydice was still in the dark.

00:01:30.462 --> 00:01:34.035
"Goodbye," she said softly, and she was gone.

00:01:34.035 --> 00:01:37.652
Orpheus sang sad songs for the rest of his life.
